# linkwarden.dadl -- Linkwarden REST API for ToolMesh
# Linkwarden is a self-hosted, open-source bookmark manager and web archive
# (AGPL-3.0). Every saved link is preserved by the server in up to five
# formats -- screenshot (PNG or JPEG), PDF, readable text, single-file HTML
# ("monolith") and optionally a Wayback Machine snapshot -- so the content
# stays available when the original page changes or disappears. Links live
# in collections (nested, shareable with other users, optionally public) and
# carry tags; full-text search runs over names, URLs, descriptions, tags and
# the archived page text.
#
# Domain Notes for LLM consumers:
# - AUTH: an access token created under Settings > Access Tokens, sent as
#   "Authorization: Bearer <token>". Tokens have no scopes: a token acts with
#   the full rights of the account that created it. The account with user
#   id 1 (or the id in the server setting NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN) is the server
#   admin; only it may list, create and delete other users.
# - BASE URL: the instance origin (https://links.example.com), without
#   /api/v1. Paths here carry the version because the dashboard lives under
#   /api/v2 while everything else is /api/v1.
# - TWO RESPONSE ENVELOPES: most routes answer {"response": <data>};
#   /api/v1/search, GET /api/v1/tags and /api/v2/dashboard answer
#   {"data": <data>, "success": true, "message": "..."}. The tools below unwrap
#   both. Errors carry the message in $.response (a plain string).
# - ERROR STATUS CODES ARE LOOSE: 401 means "not logged in" (bad or revoked
#   token, body "You must be logged in.") but also "Permission denied",
#   "Collection is not accessible." or "Please choose valid links." for an
#   object the account may not touch. A missing link answers 404 on some
#   routes, 400 ("Link not found.") on others, and get_link reports a
#   deleted link as 401 "Collection is not accessible."; get_collection
#   returns null. A read-only demo instance
#   answers every write with 400 "This action is disabled because this is a
#   read-only demo of Linkwarden."
# - IDS are integers: links, collections, tags, highlights, RSS
#   subscriptions, tokens and users each have their own id space.
# - PRESERVATION IS ASYNCHRONOUS: create_link returns at once; a background
#   worker fetches the page within seconds to minutes and fills the link
#   fields image (screenshot path), pdf, readable, monolith and preview, plus
#   textContent (the readable page text) and lastPreserved. null means "not
#   archived (yet)", the string "unavailable" means "this format failed or is
#   disabled". The account settings archiveAsScreenshot, archiveAsPDF,
#   archiveAsReadable, archiveAsMonolith and archiveAsWaybackMachine (and the
#   same flags on a tag, which override them for links carrying the tag)
#   decide which formats are made.
# - ARCHIVE FORMAT CODES (query parameter format): 0 = PNG screenshot,
#   1 = JPEG screenshot, 2 = PDF, 3 = readable (JSON from Mozilla
#   Readability: title, byline, excerpt, content as HTML, textContent),
#   4 = monolith (the whole page as one self-contained HTML file). The
#   screenshot exists as PNG or JPEG, never both. Uploads accept 0, 1, 2 and
#   4 only; readable is always generated by the server.
# - SEARCH: search_links is the listing endpoint (GET /api/v1/links is
#   deprecated and can be switched off by the operator). With Meilisearch
#   configured (standard Docker setup) searchQueryString is a query language:
#   free words, plus filters url:, name:, description:, type: (url, pdf,
#   image), collection:<name>, tag:<name>, pinned:true|false, public:true,
#   before:<date>, after:<date>; prefix a filter with ! to negate it; quote
#   values that contain spaces (tag:"read later"). The index is updated by
#   the background worker, so the query language sees edits after a few
#   seconds up to a minute; collectionId, tagId and pinnedOnly are database
#   filters and always current. Without Meilisearch the string is a plain
#   case-insensitive substring match on name, URL, description and tag
#   names. Results never contain textContent; call get_link for the page
#   text. An empty result arrives as data: [] instead of {links,
#   nextCursor}; search_links normalizes it.
# - COLLECTION BY NAME: create_link with collection {name} and
#   create_rss_subscription with collectionName always create a NEW
#   collection of that name (only "Unorganized" is reused). Use ids to file
#   into existing collections.
# - PAGING: lists return a page of PAGINATION_TAKE_COUNT items (server
#   setting, default 50) and a nextCursor; pass it back as cursor for the
#   next page, null means last page. The cursor is an opaque number (a link
#   id or an offset, depending on the search backend).
# - SORT CODES for links: 0 newest first (default), 1 oldest first,
#   2 name A-Z, 3 name Z-A, 4 custom order (only together with
#   collectionId). For tags: 0 newest, 1 oldest, 2 name A-Z, 3 name Z-A,
#   4 most links first, 5 fewest links first.
# - FULL-OBJECT UPDATES: PUT on a link, a collection and the user account
#   replaces the object: omitted fields are reset (a link's name and
#   description become empty, its tag set is replaced, a collection's
#   members are removed, the user's avatar is cleared and locale reset).
#   The composites update_link, update_collection and update_my_settings
#   read the object first and send it back with only the given fields
#   changed; the raw _update_*_raw tools exist for them.
# - COLLECTIONS: every account has an "Unorganized" collection that
#   create_link uses when no collection is given (created on first use).
#   Collections nest through parentId. Members get canCreate, canUpdate and
#   canDelete; only the owner may change or delete a collection or move
#   links into or out of it. Deleting a collection deletes its
#   sub-collections, all their links and all archived files.
# - TAGS are per owner and named; create_link, update_link and update_links
#   take tag NAMES and create missing tags on the fly. A tag can carry its
#   own archive flags (null = follow the account setting).
# - UPLOADS: upload_archive replaces one format of an existing link,
#   create_link_from_file creates a new link from a PDF, image or HTML file
#   (it lands in "Unorganized"). The size limit is NEXT_PUBLIC_MAX_FILE_BUFFER
#   (server setting, default 10 MB); bookmark imports are limited by
#   IMPORT_LIMIT (default 10 MB). Linkwarden compares the file's content
#   type exactly (image/png, image/jpeg, application/pdf, text/html): a
#   source that sends parameters ("application/pdf; qs=0.001") is refused.
# - REORDER BODY: Linkwarden rejects PUT /links/{id}/order without a JSON
#   object, and ToolMesh sends no body when no body field is set, so
#   reorder_link carries a constant field that Linkwarden ignores.
# - PARENT "root": a collection's parentId is a number or the string
#   "root" (move to the top level). A DADL param has one type, so the
#   top-level move has its own raw tool, _update_collection_root_raw.
# - NOT COVERED on purpose: password sign-in, sessions and OAuth flows,
#   access-token creation (an agent should not mint credentials), billing
#   and app-store webhooks, the internal worker routes, the user content
#   domain viewer, avatars and the favicon proxy.
# - Verified against a live Linkwarden v2.17.0 instance (2026-11).

spec: "https://dadl.ai/spec/dadl-spec-v0.2.md"

credits:
  - "Dunkel Cloud GmbH -- maintainer"

source_name: "Linkwarden REST API"
source_url: "https://docs.linkwarden.app/api/api-introduction"
date: "2026-11-27"

backend:
  name: linkwarden
  type: rest
  version: "1.0"
  # base_url intentionally omitted -- Linkwarden is self-hosted; backends.yaml
  # url supplies the instance origin (see setup.notes).
  description: "Linkwarden (self-hosted bookmark manager and web archive): links with automatic preservation as screenshot, PDF, readable text and single-file HTML; full-text search with filters; collections (nested, shared, public); tags; highlights; RSS subscriptions; bookmark import and export; users and access tokens."

  auth:
    type: bearer
    credential: linkwarden_token
    inject_into: header
    header_name: Authorization
    prefix: "Bearer "

  # GET /api/v1/users/me is small, has no side effects and fails with 401
  # for a missing, expired or revoked token. Linkwarden does not report the
  # expiry of the token in use (tokens are encrypted JWTs), so there is no
  # auth_expires_path; operators set health_check.auth_expires_at instead.
  health:
    tool: get_me
    expect_path: "$.response.id"

  defaults:
    headers:
      Accept: application/json
    errors:
      format: json
      message_path: "$.response"
      retry_on: [429, 502, 503, 504]
      terminal: [400, 401, 403, 404, 405, 409, 413]
    response:
      result_path: "$.response"

  tools:

    # =========================================================================
    # Links -- search, read, create, update, delete, order
    # =========================================================================

    search_links:
      method: GET
      path: /api/v1/search
      access: read
      description: >
        Search and list links the account can see (own and shared
        collections). Returns {links: [...], nextCursor} -- pass nextCursor
        back as cursor for the next page (null = last page); a page holds 50
        links by default. All parameters are optional; without any it lists
        all links, newest first. searchQueryString: free words plus filters
        url:, name:, description:, type:(url|pdf|image), collection:<name>,
        tag:<name>, pinned:true|false, public:true, before:<YYYY-MM-DD>,
        after:<YYYY-MM-DD>; prefix a filter with ! to negate it, quote values
        with spaces (tag:"read later"). The search index trails edits by up
        to a minute (a just-added tag may not match tag:<name> yet), while
        collectionId, tagId and pinnedOnly are read live. Without
        Meilisearch on the server the string is a plain substring match on
        name, URL, description and tag names. collectionId / tagId restrict
        to one collection or tag; pinnedOnly=true returns only links pinned
        to the dashboard. sort:
        0 newest first, 1 oldest first, 2 name A-Z, 3 name Z-A, 4 custom
        order (needs collectionId). Each link has id, name, url, description,
        type, collection, tags ({id, name}), pinnedBy (non-empty = pinned by
        you) and the archive fields image, pdf, readable, monolith, preview,
        lastPreserved (null = not archived yet). The page text
        (textContent) is not included; use get_link.
      params:
        searchQueryString: { type: string, in: query, description: "Search words and filters (see tool description)" }
        collectionId: { type: integer, in: query, description: "Only links in this collection" }
        tagId: { type: integer, in: query, description: "Only links with this tag" }
        pinnedOnly: { type: boolean, in: query, description: "true = only pinned links" }
        sort: { type: integer, in: query, description: "0 newest, 1 oldest, 2 name A-Z, 3 name Z-A, 4 custom (with collectionId)" }
        cursor: { type: integer, in: query, description: "nextCursor of the previous page" }
      response:
        result_path: "$.data"
        # An empty result comes back as data: [] instead of {links, nextCursor};
        # normalize it, and cut the tags down to id and name (their archive
        # flags are on get_tag).
        transform: |
          if type == "array" then {links: ., nextCursor: null}
          else .links |= map(.tags |= map({id, name})) end

    get_link:
      method: GET
      path: /api/v1/links/{id}
      access: read
      description: >
        Get one link by id: name, url, description, type (url, pdf, image),
        collection, tags, pinnedBy, the archive fields (image, pdf, readable,
        monolith, preview: a storage path, null = not archived yet,
        "unavailable" = failed or disabled), lastPreserved and textContent --
        the readable plain text of the archived page, which can be tens of
        kilobytes. Use download_archive for the archived files. A deleted
        link, or one in a collection the account cannot see, answers 401
        "Collection is not accessible." (not 404).
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Link id" }

    create_link:
      method: POST
      path: /api/v1/links
      access: write
      description: >
        Save a new link. Only url is needed; name is fetched from the page
        title when left out. collection: {id: <collectionId>} puts it into an
        existing collection (find ids with list_collections); {name:
        "<name>"} always CREATES a new top-level collection of that name,
        even if one with the same name exists (only "Unorganized" is
        reused); without collection the link goes to "Unorganized". tags:
        [{name: "docs"}, {name: "to-read"}] -- missing tags are created.
        type: "url" (default), "pdf" or "image". Returns the new link.
        Archiving (screenshot, PDF, readable text, single-file HTML) starts
        in the background; poll get_link until lastPreserved is set. With
        the account setting preventDuplicateLinks on, a URL the account
        already saved fails with 409 "Link already exists" (compared with
        and without "www." and a trailing slash of the new URL; a saved URL
        that itself ends in "/" is not detected, so search with url: first
        when it matters).
      params:
        url: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Address to save (max 2048 characters)" }
        name: { type: string, in: body, description: "Title; default: the page title" }
        description: { type: string, in: body, description: "Free text, max 2048 characters" }
        type: { type: string, in: body, description: "url (default), pdf or image" }
        collection: { type: object, in: body, description: "{id: number} for an existing collection; {name: string} creates a new one" }
        tags: { type: array, in: body, description: "[{name: string}], max 50 characters per name" }

    _update_link_raw:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/v1/links/{link_id}
      access: write
      description: >
        Internal: full replacement of a link (omitted name and description
        become empty, the tag list replaces all tags). Use the update_link
        composite instead.
      params:
        link_id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true }
        id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Same as link_id" }
        name: { type: string, in: body }
        url: { type: string, in: body }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
        icon: { type: string, in: body }
        iconWeight: { type: string, in: body }
        color: { type: string, in: body }
        collection: { type: object, in: body, required: true, description: "{id, ownerId} of the target collection" }
        tags: { type: array, in: body, required: true, description: "[{name}] -- the complete new tag set" }
        pinnedBy: { type: array, in: body, description: "[{id: <own user id>}] pins, [] unpins, omitted = unchanged" }

    delete_link:
      method: DELETE
      path: /api/v1/links/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: >
        Delete a link together with all its archived files (screenshot, PDF,
        readable text, single-file HTML) and highlights. Cannot be undone.
        Needs ownership of the collection or canDelete as a member.
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Link id" }

    update_links:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/v1/links
      access: write
      description: >
        Bulk edit: move several links to another collection and/or add tags.
        links: [{id: 1}, {id: 2}]. newData: {collectionId: 5, tags: [{name:
        "docs"}]} -- collectionId is optional (links stay where they are),
        tags are added. removePreviousTags=true replaces the tags instead of
        adding: with newData.tags empty or left out it REMOVES ALL TAGS of
        the listed links. Names, URLs and descriptions stay unchanged.
        Returns "All links updated successfully" or 400 "Some links failed
        to update" (the others were updated).
      params:
        links: { type: array, in: body, required: true, description: "[{id: number}]" }
        newData: { type: object, in: body, required: true, description: "{collectionId?: number, tags?: [{name}]}" }
        removePreviousTags: { type: boolean, in: body, default: false, description: "true = replace tags instead of adding" }

    delete_links:
      method: DELETE
      path: /api/v1/links
      access: dangerous
      description: >
        Delete several links at once, with all their archived files. Cannot
        be undone. linkIds: [1, 2, 3]. All links must be deletable by the
        account (owner or canDelete), otherwise nothing is deleted and the
        call fails with 401 "Collection is not accessible.".
      params:
        linkIds: { type: array, in: body, required: true, description: "Link ids" }

    reorder_link:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/v1/links/{id}/order
      access: write
      description: >
        Change the custom order of a link inside its collection (the order
        shown with sort=4). beforeId: the link (same collection) the moved
        link should end up directly below; leave it out to move the link to
        the top. Returns the updated link.
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Link to move" }
        beforeId: { type: integer, in: body, description: "Link that ends up directly above; omitted = top of the collection" }
        # Linkwarden rejects this PUT without a JSON object body, and a
        # request without any body field has no body at all. This constant
        # keeps the body an object when beforeId is left out; Linkwarden
        # ignores the field.
        nonEmptyBody: { type: boolean, in: body, default: true, description: "Constant, ignored by Linkwarden; keeps the request body a JSON object" }

    # =========================================================================
    # Archives -- preserved copies of a link (screenshot, PDF, readable,
    # single-file HTML)
    # =========================================================================

    download_archive:
      method: GET
      path: /api/v1/archives/{linkId}
      access: read
      description: >
        Download one preserved format of a link as a file; returns a
        download URL (valid 24 h) instead of the bytes. format: 0 PNG
        screenshot, 1 JPEG screenshot, 2 PDF, 3 readable (JSON with title,
        excerpt, content as HTML and textContent), 4 monolith (the page as
        one self-contained HTML file). Which formats exist is visible on the
        link: image (screenshot, ends in .png or .jpeg), pdf, readable,
        monolith. preview=true returns the small JPEG thumbnail instead. A
        format that does not exist answers 404 "File not found.". For just
        the page text, get_link's textContent is cheaper.
      params:
        linkId: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Link id" }
        format: { type: integer, in: query, required: true, description: "0 png, 1 jpeg, 2 pdf, 3 readable, 4 monolith" }
        preview: { type: boolean, in: query, description: "true = thumbnail" }
      response:
        type: file_url
        ttl: 24h

    upload_archive:
      method: POST
      path: /api/v1/archives/{linkId}
      access: write
      description: >
        Replace or add one preserved format of an existing link with your
        own file, e.g. a PDF of a paywalled article or a screenshot taken
        elsewhere. file: URL of the file (https or a tm-blob handle).
        format: 0 PNG (file must be image/png), 1 JPEG (image/jpeg), 2 PDF
        (application/pdf), 4 monolith (text/html); 3 (readable) cannot be
        uploaded. Linkwarden compares the file's content type exactly: a
        server that sends "application/pdf; qs=0.001" is refused with "Only
        ... files are accepted" -- pass such a file as a tm-blob handle with
        a plain type instead. A link whose screenshot is PNG cannot get a
        JPEG and vice versa ("PNG or JPEG file already exists."). Uploading
        a PDF marks the thumbnail (preview) "unavailable". preview=true sets
        only the thumbnail from an image. Max size: the server's
        NEXT_PUBLIC_MAX_FILE_BUFFER (default 10 MB). Returns the updated
        link.
      content_type: multipart/form-data
      max_body_size: 100MB
      params:
        linkId: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Link id" }
        format: { type: integer, in: query, required: true, description: "0 png, 1 jpeg, 2 pdf, 4 monolith" }
        preview: { type: boolean, in: query, description: "true = set only the thumbnail" }
        file: { type: file_url, in: body, required: true, description: "URL of the file to upload" }

    create_link_from_file:
      method: POST
      path: /api/v1/archives
      access: write
      description: >
        Create a new link from a file: a PDF, an image or a saved HTML page.
        file: URL of the file (https or a tm-blob handle). format: 0 PNG,
        1 JPEG, 2 PDF, 4 HTML; the file's content type must be exactly
        image/png, image/jpeg, application/pdf or text/html (a type with
        parameters such as "application/pdf; qs=0.001" is refused -- pass a
        tm-blob handle with a plain type then). url (optional): the original
        address, used for the title (without it the name stays empty). The link lands in the
        "Unorganized" collection; move it with update_link. Max size: the
        server's NEXT_PUBLIC_MAX_FILE_BUFFER (default 10 MB). Returns the
        new link.
      content_type: multipart/form-data
      max_body_size: 100MB
      params:
        format: { type: integer, in: query, required: true, description: "0 png, 1 jpeg, 2 pdf, 4 html" }
        file: { type: file_url, in: body, required: true, description: "URL of the file to upload" }
        url: { type: string, in: body, description: "Original address of the document" }

    refresh_archive:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/v1/links/{id}/archive
      access: dangerous
      description: >
        Archive a link again: DELETES all existing preserved files of the
        link first, then the background worker captures the page anew (same
        as "Refresh preserved formats" in the app). If the page has changed
        or is gone, the old copy is lost. Returns "Link is being archived."
        at once; poll get_link until lastPreserved is set again. Links
        without a web URL (uploaded files) answer "Invalid URL.".
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Link id" }

    delete_archives:
      method: DELETE
      path: /api/v1/links/archive
      access: dangerous
      description: >
        Delete the preserved files (screenshot, PDF, readable text,
        single-file HTML, thumbnail) of several links; the links themselves
        stay. Cannot be undone. The background worker re-archives links
        without archives on its next pass when the account's archive
        settings ask for it. linkIds: [1, 2]. Answers "Success." and removes
        the files right after.
      params:
        linkIds: { type: array, in: body, required: true, description: "Link ids" }

    # =========================================================================
    # Collections
    # =========================================================================

    list_collections:
      method: GET
      path: /api/v1/collections
      access: read
      description: >
        List all collections the account owns or is a member of: id, name,
        description, color, icon, parentId (null = top level), isPublic,
        ownerId, members ({userId, canCreate, canUpdate, canDelete, user}),
        _count.links. Sub-collections are separate entries; build the tree
        from parentId.
      params: {}

    get_collection:
      method: GET
      path: /api/v1/collections/{id}
      access: read
      description: >
        Get one collection by id with members and link count. Returns null
        (not an error) when the collection does not exist or the account
        has no access. List its links with search_links({collectionId}).
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Collection id" }

    create_collection:
      method: POST
      path: /api/v1/collections
      access: write
      description: >
        Create a collection. parentId makes it a sub-collection (you must own
        the parent or have full rights there). color: hex such as "#0ea5e9".
        Returns the new collection.
      params:
        name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
        color: { type: string, in: body, description: "Hex color, e.g. #0ea5e9" }
        icon: { type: string, in: body, description: "Phosphor icon name" }
        iconWeight: { type: string, in: body, description: "Icon weight, e.g. regular, bold, fill" }
        parentId: { type: integer, in: body, description: "Parent collection id" }

    _update_collection_raw:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/v1/collections/{collection_id}
      access: write
      description: >
        Internal: full replacement of a collection; the members list replaces
        all members (omitted = all members removed). Use the
        update_collection composite instead.
      params:
        collection_id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true }
        id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Same as collection_id" }
        name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
        color: { type: string, in: body }
        icon: { type: string, in: body }
        iconWeight: { type: string, in: body }
        isPublic: { type: boolean, in: body }
        parentId: { type: integer, in: body, description: "Move under this collection; omitted = parent unchanged" }
        members: { type: array, in: body, required: true, description: "[{userId, canCreate, canUpdate, canDelete}] -- the complete member list" }
        propagateToSubcollections: { type: boolean, in: body }

    # Linkwarden takes parentId as a number or as the string "root" (move to
    # the top level). A DADL param has one type, so the top-level move gets
    # its own raw tool with the constant "root".
    _update_collection_root_raw:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/v1/collections/{collection_id}
      access: write
      description: >
        Internal: full replacement of a collection that also moves it to the
        top level. Use the update_collection composite with parentId "root"
        instead.
      params:
        collection_id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true }
        id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Same as collection_id" }
        name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
        color: { type: string, in: body }
        icon: { type: string, in: body }
        iconWeight: { type: string, in: body }
        isPublic: { type: boolean, in: body }
        parentId: { type: string, in: body, default: "root", description: "Constant \"root\"" }
        members: { type: array, in: body, required: true, description: "[{userId, canCreate, canUpdate, canDelete}] -- the complete member list" }
        propagateToSubcollections: { type: boolean, in: body }

    delete_collection:
      method: DELETE
      path: /api/v1/collections/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: >
        Owner: deletes the collection, ALL its sub-collections, all their
        links and all archived files. Cannot be undone. Member: only leaves
        the collection (nothing is deleted). Returns the deleted collection.
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Collection id" }

    # =========================================================================
    # Tags
    # =========================================================================

    list_tags:
      method: GET
      path: /api/v1/tags
      access: read
      description: >
        List the account's tags and the tags on links in shared collections.
        Returns {tags: [...], nextCursor}; each tag has id, name, ownerId,
        the archive flags (null = follow the account setting) and
        _count.links. search: substring of the name (case-insensitive).
        sort: 0 newest, 1 oldest, 2 name A-Z, 3 name Z-A, 4 most links
        first, 5 fewest links first. 50 tags per page; pass nextCursor back
        as cursor (null = last page).
      params:
        search: { type: string, in: query, description: "Name contains" }
        sort: { type: integer, in: query, description: "0 newest, 1 oldest, 2 A-Z, 3 Z-A, 4 most links, 5 fewest links" }
        cursor: { type: integer, in: query, description: "nextCursor of the previous page" }
      response:
        result_path: "$.data"

    get_tag:
      method: GET
      path: /api/v1/tags/{id}
      access: read
      description: "Get one tag by id: name, archive flags and _count.links. List its links with search_links({tagId})."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Tag id" }

    create_tags:
      method: POST
      path: /api/v1/tags
      access: write
      description: >
        Create tags, or update the archive settings of existing tags with
        the same name (matched by label). tags: [{label: "docs"}, {label:
        "video", archiveAsPDF: false, archiveAsScreenshot: true}]. Archive
        flags per tag: archiveAsScreenshot, archiveAsMonolith, archiveAsPDF,
        archiveAsReadable, archiveAsWaybackMachine -- true/false override the
        account setting for links with this tag, null follows it. Labels max
        50 characters. Returns the created or updated tags.
      params:
        tags: { type: array, in: body, required: true, description: "[{label, archiveAs*?}]" }

    update_tag:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/v1/tags/{id}
      access: write
      description: "Rename a tag (max 50 characters); all links keep it. Fails if the account already has a tag with that name -- use merge_tags then. Returns the tag."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Tag id" }
        name: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "New name" }

    delete_tag:
      method: DELETE
      path: /api/v1/tags/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete a tag; it is removed from all links (the links stay). Cannot be undone."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Tag id" }

    delete_tags:
      method: DELETE
      path: /api/v1/tags
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete several tags at once; they are removed from all links (the links stay). Cannot be undone. tagIds: [1, 2]. Returns the number of deleted tags."
      params:
        tagIds: { type: array, in: body, required: true, description: "Tag ids" }

    merge_tags:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/v1/tags/merge
      access: dangerous
      description: >
        Merge tags: every link carrying one of tagIds gets the tag
        newTagName (created if it does not exist), then the old tags are
        DELETED. Use it to fold duplicates ("js", "javascript") into one
        tag. Cannot be undone. Returns the resulting tag.
      params:
        tagIds: { type: array, in: body, required: true, description: "Tags to fold in" }
        newTagName: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Name of the resulting tag" }

    # =========================================================================
    # Highlights -- marked passages in the readable view
    # =========================================================================

    list_highlights:
      method: GET
      path: /api/v1/links/{id}/highlights
      access: read
      description: "List the highlights (marked text passages with optional comment) of a link: id, color, text, comment, startOffset, endOffset, userId."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Link id" }

    create_highlight:
      method: POST
      path: /api/v1/highlights
      access: write
      description: >
        Highlight a passage of a link's readable text, optionally with a
        comment. startOffset/endOffset are character offsets into the
        readable view; a highlight with the same link and offsets is updated
        (color, comment) instead of duplicated. color: yellow, red, blue or
        green (the app's colors; other strings are stored as given).
        Returns the highlight.
      params:
        linkId: { type: integer, in: body, required: true }
        text: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "The highlighted text, max 2048 characters" }
        startOffset: { type: integer, in: body, required: true }
        endOffset: { type: integer, in: body, required: true }
        color: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "yellow, red, blue or green" }
        comment: { type: string, in: body, description: "Note, max 2048 characters" }

    delete_highlight:
      method: DELETE
      path: /api/v1/highlights/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete a highlight. Cannot be undone."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Highlight id" }

    # =========================================================================
    # RSS subscriptions -- feeds whose new entries are saved as links
    # =========================================================================

    list_rss_subscriptions:
      method: GET
      path: /api/v1/rss
      access: read
      description: "List the account's RSS subscriptions: id, name, url, collectionId, collection.name, lastBuildDate. New feed entries are saved as links into the collection."
      params: {}

    create_rss_subscription:
      method: POST
      path: /api/v1/rss
      access: write
      description: >
        Subscribe to an RSS or Atom feed: the server reads it right away and
        then polls it (every 60 minutes by default), saving new entries as
        links. collectionId puts them into an existing collection,
        collectionName creates a new collection of that name; give one of
        the two. name max 50 characters. Default limit: 20 subscriptions per
        account. Returns the subscription. A URL that is not a readable feed
        (an HTML page, a 404) fails with HTTP 500, but Linkwarden may have
        stored the subscription already: check list_rss_subscriptions and
        delete it.
      params:
        name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        url: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Feed URL" }
        collectionId: { type: integer, in: body }
        collectionName: { type: string, in: body, description: "Creates a new collection" }

    delete_rss_subscription:
      method: DELETE
      path: /api/v1/rss/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete an RSS subscription. Links saved from the feed stay."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Subscription id" }

    # =========================================================================
    # Account, dashboard, tokens, users
    # =========================================================================

    get_me:
      method: GET
      path: /api/v1/users/me
      access: read
      description: >
        The account behind the token: id, username, name, email, locale,
        archive settings (archiveAsScreenshot, archiveAsMonolith,
        archiveAsPDF, archiveAsReadable, archiveAsWaybackMachine),
        preventDuplicateLinks, linksRouteTo, AI tagging settings and
        dashboardSections. Also the cheapest check that the token works.
      params: {}

    _update_user_raw:
      method: PUT
      path: /api/v1/users/{id}
      access: admin
      description: >
        Internal: full replacement of the account settings (an omitted
        image clears the avatar, an omitted locale resets it to en). Use the
        update_my_settings composite instead.
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true }
        username: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        name: { type: string, in: body }
        email: { type: string, in: body }
        image: { type: string, in: body }
        locale: { type: string, in: body }
        archiveAsScreenshot: { type: boolean, in: body }
        archiveAsMonolith: { type: boolean, in: body }
        archiveAsPDF: { type: boolean, in: body }
        archiveAsReadable: { type: boolean, in: body }
        archiveAsWaybackMachine: { type: boolean, in: body }
        preventDuplicateLinks: { type: boolean, in: body }
        linksRouteTo: { type: string, in: body }
        aiTaggingMethod: { type: string, in: body }
        aiPredefinedTags: { type: array, in: body }
        aiTagExistingLinks: { type: boolean, in: body }

    get_dashboard:
      method: GET
      path: /api/v2/dashboard
      access: read
      description: >
        The dashboard: {links, collectionLinks, numberOfPinnedLinks,
        numberOfTags} -- links holds up to 16 recent and up to 16 pinned
        links, collectionLinks up to 16 links per collection shown on the
        dashboard (keyed by collection id). Links come without textContent.
      params: {}
      response:
        result_path: "$.data"

    list_tokens:
      method: GET
      path: /api/v1/tokens
      access: read
      description: "List the account's access tokens and app sessions: id, name, isSession, expires, createdAt. Never returns the secret. Use it to see when a token expires."
      params: {}

    revoke_token:
      method: DELETE
      path: /api/v1/tokens/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Revoke an access token or app session by id (from list_tokens). Revoking the token this backend uses locks it out until a new token is configured. Returns the revoked token entry (revoked: true)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Token id" }
      response:
        result_path: "$.response"
        # The answer carries the token's internal identifier (field token),
        # which list_tokens never shows; leave it out here too.
        transform: "del(.token)"

    list_users:
      method: GET
      path: /api/v1/users
      access: admin
      description: "Server admin only: list all user accounts (id, username, email, emailVerified, createdAt). Other accounts get 404 \"Subscription not found.\" or only their subscription's members."
      params: {}

    create_user:
      method: POST
      path: /api/v1/users
      access: admin
      description: >
        Create a user account (server admin; also open to anyone while
        registration is enabled). username: 3-50 characters of a-z, 0-9, _
        and -. password: at least 8 characters. On instances with e-mail
        configured, email is required instead of username. Returns the new
        account (HTTP 201).
      params:
        username: { type: string, in: body }
        password: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        name: { type: string, in: body }
        email: { type: string, in: body }

    delete_user:
      method: DELETE
      path: /api/v1/users/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Server admin: delete a user account with all its collections, links, archived files and tags. Cannot be undone."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "User id" }

    # =========================================================================
    # Import, export, instance
    # =========================================================================

    export_data:
      method: GET
      path: /api/v1/migration
      access: read
      description: >
        Export everything of the account (collections, links with tags and
        page text, settings) as Linkwarden backup JSON; returns a download
        URL (valid 24 h). The file can be re-imported with import_bookmarks
        format 0. Archived files (screenshots, PDFs) are not included.
      params: {}
      response:
        type: file_url
        ttl: 24h

    import_bookmarks:
      method: POST
      path: /api/v1/migration
      access: write
      description: >
        Import bookmarks into the account; the imported links are archived
        in the background. format: 0 Linkwarden backup JSON, 1 browser
        bookmarks HTML (Netscape format, as exported by Chrome, Firefox,
        Safari, Edge), 2 Wallabag JSON, 3 Omnivore, 4 Pocket. data: the file
        content as a string. Folders become collections. Max size: the
        server's IMPORT_LIMIT (default 10 MB).
      params:
        format: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "0 linkwarden, 1 html, 2 wallabag, 3 omnivore, 4 pocket" }
        data: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "File content" }

    get_instance_config:
      method: GET
      path: /api/v1/config
      access: read
      description: "Public instance settings: INSTANCE_VERSION, DISABLE_REGISTRATION, MAX_FILE_BUFFER (MB), RSS_POLLING_INTERVAL_MINUTES, AI_ENABLED, EMAIL_PROVIDER, ADMIN (admin user id), USER_CONTENT_DOMAIN. null = server default. Needs no token."
      params: {}

  composites:

    update_link:
      access: write
      description: >
        Update a link; only the given fields change, everything else is kept
        (reads the link first). name, url, description; collectionId moves
        the link (you must own both collections); tags: list of names
        ["docs", "to-read"] that REPLACES the tag set (missing tags are
        created; [] removes all); pinned: true pins the link to your
        dashboard, false unpins; icon, iconWeight, color for the link's own
        icon. Changing url drops the archived files and archives anew.
        Returns the updated link.
      params:
        id: { type: number, required: true, description: "Link id" }
        name: { type: string }
        url: { type: string }
        description: { type: string }
        collectionId: { type: number, description: "Move to this collection" }
        tags: { type: array, description: "Tag names; replaces the tag set" }
        pinned: { type: boolean }
        icon: { type: string }
        iconWeight: { type: string }
        color: { type: string }
      timeout: 30s
      depends_on: [get_link, get_collection, get_me, _update_link_raw]
      code: |
        const cur = await api.get_link({ id: params.id });
        if (!cur || !cur.collection) throw new Error("Link not found: " + params.id);
        const keep = (k) => (params[k] !== undefined ? params[k] : cur[k]);
        let collection = { id: cur.collection.id, ownerId: cur.collection.ownerId };
        if (params.collectionId !== undefined && params.collectionId !== cur.collection.id) {
          const target = await api.get_collection({ id: params.collectionId });
          if (!target) throw new Error("Collection not found or not accessible: " + params.collectionId);
          collection = { id: target.id, ownerId: target.ownerId };
        }
        const tags = params.tags !== undefined
          ? params.tags.map((t) => (typeof t === "string" ? { name: t } : { name: t.name }))
          : (cur.tags || []).map((t) => ({ name: t.name }));
        const body = {
          link_id: params.id,
          id: params.id,
          name: keep("name") || "",
          description: keep("description") || "",
          collection: collection,
          tags: tags,
        };
        const url = keep("url");
        if (url !== null && url !== undefined) body.url = url;
        for (const k of ["icon", "iconWeight", "color"]) {
          const v = keep(k);
          if (v !== null && v !== undefined) body[k] = v;
        }
        if (params.pinned !== undefined) {
          const me = await api.get_me();
          body.pinnedBy = params.pinned ? [{ id: me.id }] : [];
        }
        return await api._update_link_raw(body);

    update_collection:
      access: write
      description: >
        Update a collection; only the given fields change, everything else
        (including members) is kept. name, description, color, icon,
        iconWeight; parentId: a collection id to move it under, or "root"
        to move it to the top level; isPublic: true makes the collection and
        its links readable by anyone with the link, false makes it private
        again; members: [{userId, canCreate, canUpdate, canDelete}] REPLACES
        the member list ([] removes everyone); propagateToSubcollections:
        true copies the member list to all sub-collections. Owner only.
        Returns the updated collection.
      params:
        id: { type: number, required: true, description: "Collection id" }
        name: { type: string }
        description: { type: string }
        color: { type: string }
        icon: { type: string }
        iconWeight: { type: string }
        parentId: { type: string, description: "Collection id, or \"root\"" }
        isPublic: { type: boolean }
        members: { type: array, description: "[{userId, canCreate, canUpdate, canDelete}]" }
        propagateToSubcollections: { type: boolean }
      timeout: 30s
      depends_on: [get_collection, _update_collection_raw, _update_collection_root_raw]
      code: |
        const cur = await api.get_collection({ id: params.id });
        if (!cur) throw new Error("Collection not found or not accessible: " + params.id);
        const keep = (k) => (params[k] !== undefined ? params[k] : cur[k]);
        const members = params.members !== undefined
          ? params.members
          : (cur.members || []).map((m) => ({
              userId: m.userId,
              canCreate: m.canCreate,
              canUpdate: m.canUpdate,
              canDelete: m.canDelete,
            }));
        const body = { collection_id: params.id, id: params.id, name: keep("name"), members: members };
        for (const k of ["description", "color", "icon", "iconWeight", "isPublic"]) {
          const v = keep(k);
          if (v !== null && v !== undefined) body[k] = v;
        }
        if (params.propagateToSubcollections !== undefined) body.propagateToSubcollections = params.propagateToSubcollections;
        if (params.parentId !== undefined && params.parentId !== null && String(params.parentId) !== "") {
          const p = String(params.parentId);
          if (p === "root") return await api._update_collection_root_raw(body);
          const n = Number(p);
          if (!Number.isInteger(n)) throw new Error("parentId must be a collection id or \"root\": " + p);
          body.parentId = n;
        }
        return await api._update_collection_raw(body);

    update_my_settings:
      access: admin
      description: >
        Change settings of the account behind the token; only the given
        fields change. name; locale (e.g. en, de, fr); the archive formats
        made for new links: archiveAsScreenshot, archiveAsPDF,
        archiveAsReadable, archiveAsMonolith, archiveAsWaybackMachine
        (booleans); preventDuplicateLinks (true = create_link refuses a URL
        that is already saved); linksRouteTo (what opening a link shows:
        ORIGINAL, PDF, READABLE, MONOLITH, SCREENSHOT, DETAILS);
        aiTaggingMethod (DISABLED, GENERATE, EXISTING, PREDEFINED),
        aiPredefinedTags (up to 20 names), aiTagExistingLinks -- AI tagging
        works only when the server has a model configured. Username, e-mail
        and password are not changed here. Returns the account.
      params:
        name: { type: string }
        locale: { type: string }
        archiveAsScreenshot: { type: boolean }
        archiveAsMonolith: { type: boolean }
        archiveAsPDF: { type: boolean }
        archiveAsReadable: { type: boolean }
        archiveAsWaybackMachine: { type: boolean }
        preventDuplicateLinks: { type: boolean }
        linksRouteTo: { type: string }
        aiTaggingMethod: { type: string }
        aiPredefinedTags: { type: array }
        aiTagExistingLinks: { type: boolean }
      timeout: 30s
      depends_on: [get_me, _update_user_raw]
      code: |
        const me = await api.get_me();
        const body = { id: me.id, username: me.username, locale: me.locale };
        if (me.name !== null && me.name !== undefined) body.name = me.name;
        if (me.email) body.email = me.email;
        if (me.image) body.image = me.image.split("?")[0];
        const fields = [
          "name", "locale", "archiveAsScreenshot", "archiveAsMonolith", "archiveAsPDF",
          "archiveAsReadable", "archiveAsWaybackMachine", "preventDuplicateLinks",
          "linksRouteTo", "aiTaggingMethod", "aiPredefinedTags", "aiTagExistingLinks",
        ];
        for (const k of fields) {
          if (params[k] !== undefined) body[k] = params[k];
        }
        return await api._update_user_raw(body);

  examples:
    - name: "Save a link and wait for the archive"
      description: "Create a link in a collection with tags, then read its readable text once the background archiving is done"
      code: |
        const cols = await api.list_collections();
        const research = cols.find((c) => c.name === "Research");
        const link = await api.create_link({
          url: "https://example.com/article",
          collection: research ? { id: research.id } : { name: "Research" },
          tags: [{ name: "to-read" }],
        });
        const cur = await api.get_link({ id: link.id });
        if (!cur.lastPreserved) return { id: link.id, status: "archiving, check again later" };
        return { id: cur.id, name: cur.name, text: (cur.textContent || "").slice(0, 2000) };

    - name: "Tidy up search results"
      description: "Find untagged-looking links about a topic and add a tag to all of them in one call"
      code: |
        const page = await api.search_links({ searchQueryString: "kubernetes !tag:k8s" });
        const ids = page.links.map((l) => ({ id: l.id }));
        if (ids.length === 0) return "nothing to tag";
        await api.update_links({ links: ids, newData: { tags: [{ name: "k8s" }] } });
        return ids.length + " links tagged";

  coverage:
    endpoints: 43
    total_endpoints: 74
    percentage: 57
    focus: >
      Linkwarden API v1: links (search with filters, create, update, pin,
      move, bulk edit, custom order), archives (screenshot, PDF, readable
      text, single-file HTML, upload, refresh), collections (nested, shared,
      public), tags (rename, merge, bulk delete), highlights, RSS
      subscriptions, bookmark import and export, account settings, users,
      access tokens.
    missing: >
      Sign-in, sessions and OAuth flows, password reset and e-mail
      verification; access-token creation (not exposed on purpose); billing,
      payment and app-store webhooks; internal worker routes; the user
      content domain viewer; public (unauthenticated) collection, link, tag
      and user views; avatars and the favicon proxy; get user by id, user
      preferences (theme, reader font); dashboard layout editing; the
      deprecated GET /api/v1/links and v1 dashboard.
    last_reviewed: "2026-11-27"

  setup:
    credential_steps:
      - "Sign in to Linkwarden, open Settings > Access Tokens and create a new token. Pick an expiry: 7 days, 30, 60 or 90 days, or never."
      - "Copy the token right away; Linkwarden shows it only once."
      - "Tokens have no scopes: the token can do everything the account can. For read-mostly use create a separate account and share collections with it as a member without update or delete rights. User management (list_users, create_user, delete_user) needs the server admin account."
      - "Put the token into the ToolMesh .env as CREDENTIAL_LINKWARDEN_TOKEN and add the backends.yaml entry with your instance URL."
    env_var: CREDENTIAL_LINKWARDEN_TOKEN
    backends_yaml: |
      - name: linkwarden
        transport: rest
        dadl: linkwarden.dadl
        url: "https://links.example.com"
    required_scopes:
      - "Access token of a Linkwarden account (tokens carry the account's full rights)"
    optional_scopes:
      - "Server admin account for user management"
    docs_url: "https://docs.linkwarden.app/api/api-introduction"
    notes: >
      Set url to the origin of your instance (https://links.example.com),
      without /api/v1: the tools carry the version in their paths because
      the dashboard lives under /api/v2. Linkwarden Cloud works the same
      way with url https://cloud.linkwarden.app. Linkwarden does not report
      the expiry of the token in use; list_tokens shows it, and you can put
      it into backends.yaml as health_check.auth_expires_at so ToolMesh warns
      before it runs out. Archiving needs the browser bundled in the
      official Docker image; the search query language (tag:, collection:,
      before:, ...) needs Meilisearch, which the official docker-compose
      setup includes. Verified against Linkwarden v2.17.0.
